      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): include sender in duplicate-user-message dedup key",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMulti-user session compaction dedup collapses messages from different senders when they happen to send the same long text within the 60-second window, silently dropping a distinct participant's turn.\n\n- **Problem**: `duplicateSignature()` builds the dedup key from normalized text only, ignoring sender identity. Alice and Bob both saying \"please run the deployment status check for production\" within 60s → Bob's message is dropped.\n- **Solution**: Include `__openclaw.senderId` in the dedup key so same text from different senders is kept.\n- **Prerequisite**: #90552 landed `senderId`/`senderName`/`senderUsername` in the `__openclaw` envelope on user-turn transcript messages.\n- **What changed**: `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compaction-duplicate-user-messages.ts` (add `__openclaw` to `MessageLike`, read `senderId` in dedup key), test file (3 new test cases)\n- **What did NOT change**: Same-sender retry dedup behavior; short message dedup (<24 chars); compaction summary generation; messages without sender metadata (direct chats, legacy transcripts)\n\n## Change Type (select all)\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n- [ ] Feature\n- [ ] Refactor required for the fix\n- [ ] Docs\n- [ ] Security hardening\n- [ ] Chore/infra\n\n## Scope (select all)\n\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\n- [x] Skills / tool execution\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\n- [x] Memory / storage\n- [ ] Integrations\n- [ ] API / contracts\n- [ ] UI / DX\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\n\n## Linked Issue/PR\n\n- Related to #98310\n- Depends on #90552\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\n\n## Motivation\n\nCompaction dedup was designed to fold \"single-user retries\" (same person re-sending the same long message within a short window). Without sender identity, it silently over-collapses distinct group participants who independently send identical text.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Behavior addressed**: Same text from different senders within the dedup window is now preserved for each sender\n- **Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22, branch `fix/compaction-duplicate-user-sender-98310` on upstream/main (f296dc4e68)\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n\n```console\n$ pnpm test src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compaction-duplicate-user-messages.test.ts --reporter verbose\n```\n\n- **Evidence after fix**:\n\n```console\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  6 passed (6)\n\nBefore: duplicateSignature(\"alice\", \"run deployment...\") == duplicateSignature(\"bob\", \"run deployment...\")\nAfter:  duplicateSignature(\"alice\", \"run deployment...\") != duplicateSignature(\"bob\", \"run deployment...\")\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix**:\n  1. Same sender, same text, inside window → still deduped (existing behavior)\n  2. Different sender, same text, inside window → both kept (bug fixed)\n  3. No senderId on message → empty prefix, dedup by text alone (existing behavior)\n  4. All 6 tests pass, 3 existing + 3 new\n- **What was not tested**: Real multi-user compaction E2E flow; non-user messages in dedup path\n\n## Root Cause (if applicable)\n\nIn `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compaction-duplicate-user-messages.ts:47-59`, the `duplicateSignature()` function builds a dedup key from `text.normalize(\"NFC\").toLowerCase()` alone, with no sender component. Two different users sending the same normalized text within `DEFAULT_DUPLICATE_USER_MESSAGE_WINDOW_MS` (60s) produce the same key, and the second message is silently dropped.\n\nPrevious attempt used `senderIsOwner` (boolean) — insufficient because two distinct non-owner participants (both `senderIsOwner: false`) still collided. The correct approach requires `senderId` from `__openclaw`, which required #90552 to land first.\n\n## User-visible / Behavior Changes\n\nMulti-user sessions no longer lose a participant's message when another user happens to send the same text within 60 seconds.\n\n## Security Impact (required)\n\n- [x] New permissions/capabilities? No\n- [x] Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\n- [x] New/changed network calls? No\n- [x] Command/tool execution surface changed? No\n- [x] Data access scope changed? No\n\n## Best-fix Verdict\n\n- **Best fix**: Yes. Using `__openclaw.senderId` (string) as the dedup key prefix is the minimal correct fix — it preserves existing same-sender dedup while preventing cross-sender over-collapse with true per-participant identity.\n- **Refactor needed**: No\n- **Alternative considered**: Removing dedup entirely — rejected because same-sender retries are genuine compaction artifacts worth folding.\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding of code changes**: Yes\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n- **Highest risk area**: Messages from senders without a `senderId` field default to empty string key prefix, keeping existing behavior for unlabeled messages.\n- **Mitigation**: `senderId` is optional — when absent/undefined, the key defaults to `|text`, which means unlabeled messages still collapse into each other (same as before).\n- **Compatibility**: Fully backward compatible — only cross-sender dedup behavior changes, messages without sender metadata are unaffected.\n\n---\n\nRelated to #98310\nDepends on #90552",
